From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Track held keys before the modal console can take them

The control keeps the set of keys that are physically down, and gnoblin.input.grab refuses to
start while the set is not empty. The set was fed from gnoblin_native_control_filter_input_event,
which the stage input-policy filter reaches only after the diagnostic console has declined a key.
While the console is open it takes every key press and release, so a key released under the
console never left the set, and every later grab was refused until the user tapped that key.

Offer each event to the control's key tracking first, ahead of the console.

diff --git a/src/core/events.c b/src/core/events.c
--- a/src/core/events.c
+++ b/src/core/events.c
@@ -429,6 +429,10 @@ gnoblin_input_policy_stage_filter (ClutterStage       *stage,
   MetaDisplay *display = user_data;
 
   (void) stage;
+  /* The set of held keys sees every key press and release first, also the ones the console takes
+   * just below. A release that the console swallowed would otherwise leave its key held for
+   * ever, and every keyboard grab would be refused. */
+  gnoblin_native_control_track_key (display, event);
   /* The diagnostic console is modal: while it is open it takes key events before Lua input
    * handlers, keybindings and shortcuts can act on them. */
   if (gnoblin_plugin_input_handle_key (G_OBJECT (display), event))
